{"name":"Simply Peachy","hex":"#ffc06c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"simply","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["In a simple way or state; considered in or by itself; without addition; alone.","Plainly; without art or subtlety."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/simply"},{"term":"peachy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Resembling a peach, peach-like.","Very good, excellent, typically used sarcastically to indicate a state of misery, resentment or great frustration."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peachy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Peachy","blocks":[{"text":"\"Peachy\" is a song by Australian singer-songwriter Missy Higgins and the third single released from her second album, On A Clear Night. The track features a guest appearance by Neil Finn playing electric guitar. The single was released on 10 November 2007, as a digital download only. At the ARIA Music Awards of 2008 Higgins was nominated for Best Female Artist for this single."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/71/MissyHiggins_Peachy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peachy"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"simply":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/92/En-us-simply.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/92/En-us-simply.ogg/En-us-simply.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/35/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Wodencafe-simply.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/35/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Wodencafe-simply.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Wodencafe-simply.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","sr